# Apero Node.js project — local dev env.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored — NEVER commit it.
# In prod the same vars are injected by the deploy platform, NOT from this file.
#
# This file is shape-agnostic. HTTP-service / SSO vars live in
# shapes/http-service/env-additions.txt — append them when you apply that shape.

# --- App ---
APP_NAME=apero-project
APP_ENV=local

# --- Logging ---
# debug | info | warn | error
LOG_LEVEL=info

# --- Secrets ---
# Secrets live here in plain form and are read directly via src/config.ts
# (getConfig().SECRET_OPENAI_API_KEY). One SECRET_* var per secret, mirrored as a
# ConfigSchema field. Uncomment what you need and paste the real value:
# SECRET_OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-real-key-here
# SECRET_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=...apps.googleusercontent.com
# SECRET_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-...
#
# Keep real values OUT of git — `.env` is gitignored; never commit it, never paste
# values into chat / tickets / Slack. A shared secret store (Vault) is a deferred,
# future option — not required today. See docs/vault.md.
